---
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Overcut™ — serious driving, shared strategy';
const description =
	'A collisionless competitive circuit racer with equal cars, distinct driver abilities, and team-first strategy. A playable concept in development.';

const principles = [
	{
		name: 'No contact',
		statement: 'Your race is yours.',
		copy: 'Player cars never collide. Another driver cannot erase your race with one missed braking point.',
		className: 'principle-acid',
	},
	{
		name: 'Equal cars',
		statement: 'No setup advantage.',
		copy: 'Every car performs identically. Liveries change identity, not the machinery underneath.',
		className: 'principle-cyan',
	},
	{
		name: 'Team result',
		statement: 'Finish together.',
		copy: 'Individual places still matter, but the team competes to leave the race with the most points.',
		className: 'principle-violet',
	},
];

const consequences = [
	['Brake too late', 'Lose the corner.'],
	['Overwork the tires', 'Lose the stint.'],
	['Miss the pit box', 'Lose time.'],
	['Hit the barrier', 'Rejoin the fight.'],
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/">
	<!--
		THESIS: Serious racing can remove contact and setup inequality without removing consequence.
		OWN-WORLD: Aldermoor race-programme typography, blue night surfaces, acid series signals,
		photoreal hardware, and painted people; never synthwave.
		STORY: Understand the fair-competition concept, see how abilities create team strategy, and
		follow the build.
		FIRST VIEWPORT: Text-safe circuit hero, car right, emphatic promise left, build action visible.
		FORM: Long-form race programme; editorial sections alternate with trackside principle bands.
	-->
	<SiteHeader />

	<main id="main-content">
		<Hero />

		<section id="concept" class="concept section-shell" aria-labelledby="concept-title">
			<div class="concept-title">
				<h2 id="concept-title" class="display-heading">Keep the race. Cut the collision.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="concept-copy body-copy">
				<p>
					Overcut starts with serious racing fundamentals: learn the circuit, manage the
					car, execute the stop, and find speed where someone else cannot.
				</p>
				<p>
					Then it makes deliberate tradeoffs. <strong>Player cars cannot collide.</strong>{' '}
					Every driver gets equal-performance machinery. A mistake costs time, but another
					driver's mistake does not get to decide whether your race continues.
				</p>
				<p>
					The result is not a softer race. It is a race that asks more useful questions:
					how well can you drive, what strategy can your team execute, and what can you
					still contribute when the perfect result is gone?
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="principles" aria-label="Overcut's three competitive principles">
			{principles.map((principle) => (
				<article class:list={['principle', principle.className]}>
					<div class="shell principle-inner">
						<p class="principle-name">{principle.name}</p>
						<h2>{principle.statement}</h2>
						<p>{principle.copy}</p>
					</div>
				</article>
			))}
		</section>

		<section id="abilities" class="abilities" aria-labelledby="abilities-title">
			<div class="abilities-art">
				<img
					src="/images/overcut-drivers.webp"
					alt="Painted concept art of a group of Overcut drivers in distinct racing suits"
					width="1536"
					height="1024"
					loading="lazy"
					decoding="async"
				/>
			</div>

			<div class="section-shell abilities-layout">
				<div class="abilities-content">
					<h2 id="abilities-title" class="display-heading">
						Drivers bring more than a racing line.
					</h2>

					<div class="body-copy">
						<p>
							Like the agents in VALORANT, Overcut's drivers are defined in part by
							distinct abilities. The comparison is structural: abilities create choices,
							roles, and moments for coordinated play.
						</p>
						<p>
							Overcut draws a hard line around what those abilities can do.{' '}
							<strong>They help you or your teammates. They never hinder a rival.</strong>{' '}
							No weapons. No blue shells. No button that ruins somebody else's race.
						</p>
						<p>
							The exact effects, triggers, charge rules, and loadouts are still being
							designed. The principle is settled. The implementation is not.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="consequences section-shell" aria-labelledby="consequences-title">
			<div>
				<h2 id="consequences-title" class="display-heading">
					Your mistakes still matter.
				</h2>
				<p class="body-copy consequences-intro">
					Collisionless does not mean consequence-free. Overcut protects the race from
					contact, not the driver from the clock.
				</p>
			</div>

			<dl class="consequence-list">
				{consequences.map(([mistake, cost]) => (
					<div>
						<dt>{mistake}</dt>
						<dd>{cost}</dd>
					</div>
				))}
			</dl>
		</section>

		<section class="machinery" aria-labelledby="machinery-title">
			<div class="shell machinery-layout">
				<div class="machinery-art">
					<img
						src="/images/overcut-liveries.webp"
						alt="Concept lineup of four identical Overcut cars wearing different liveries"
						width="1536"
						height="1024"
						loading="lazy"
						decoding="async"
					/>
					<p>Concept art. Liveries vary; performance does not.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="machinery-copy">
					<h2 id="machinery-title" class="display-heading">One car. A grid of identities.</h2>
					<div class="body-copy">
						<p>
							Sim racing often rewards hours spent tuning a setup for one car, circuit,
							and condition. Overcut removes that homework from the competition.
						</p>
						<p>
							Every car starts on equal footing. Teams and drivers can look distinct,
							but a faster livery does not exist. The advantage has to come from the
							people inside the cars and the choices they make together.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section id="purpose" class="purpose section-shell" aria-labelledby="purpose-title">
			<div class="purpose-question">
				<h2 id="purpose-title">
					Can serious racing be easier to enter and easier to return to
					<span>without becoming less competitive?</span>
				</h2>
			</div>

			<div class="purpose-copy body-copy">
				<p>
					That is the question Overcut exists to answer. It is a playable concept, not a
					promise to become every kind of racing game.
				</p>
				<p>
					It comes from wanting a game with sim racing in its bones that does not demand
					a perfect schedule, a perfect setup, or a contact-free field just to make one
					evening of competition worthwhile.
				</p>
				<p>
					If collisionless racing, equal machinery, driver abilities, and team scoring
					work together, the concept earns the right to keep growing. The point is to
					prove that idea by making it playable.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="commitments" aria-labelledby="commitments-title">
			<div class="section-shell">
				<h2 id="commitments-title" class="display-heading">Built in public. Honest about the build.</h2>

				<div class="commitment-grid">
					<article>
						<h3>One programmer, one playable idea</h3>
						<p>
							Overcut is a solo-built concept focused on testing its central racing
							ideas. Development progress, tradeoffs, and lessons live in the build
							journal.
						</p>
					</article>

					<article>
						<h3>AI-generated concept art, clearly labeled</h3>
						<p>
							The project uses AI-generated art because its creator is a programmer,
							not a visual artist. While it does, Overcut will remain free to play and
							will not be monetized.
						</p>
					</article>

					<article>
						<h3>A grid more people can see themselves in</h3>
						<p>
							Racing has not represented everyone equally. Overcut intends to build a
							broader cast while treating representation as work to keep doing, not a
							box already checked.
						</p>
					</article>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="follow-title">
			<div class="section-shell final-cta-inner">
				<div>
					<h2 id="follow-title" class="display-heading">Follow the build, not a release countdown.</h2>
					<p>
						Overcut is in development. The journal covers what changes, what fails, and
						what the playable concept proves next.
					</p>
				</div>
				<a class="action action-primary" href="https://caseyirvine.dev">
					Read the development series <span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span>
				</a>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>

	<SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.concept {
		display: grid;
		gap: 3rem;
	}

	.concept-copy {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.4rem;
	}

	.concept-copy p,
	.abilities-content p,
	.machinery-copy p,
	.purpose-copy p {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.principles {
		border-block: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-paper) 18%, transparent);
	}

	.principle {
		position: relative;
		overflow: hidden;
		border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-paper) 18%, transparent);
	}

	.principle:last-child {
		border-bottom: 0;
	}

	.principle::before {
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0 0 auto;
		height: 2px;
		background: var(--principle-color);
		content: "";
	}

	.principle-acid {
		--principle-color: var(--color-acid);
	}

	.principle-cyan {
		--principle-color: var(--color-cyan);
	}

	.principle-violet {
		--principle-color: var(--color-violet);
	}

	.principle-inner {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		align-items: center;
		padding-block: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
	}

	.principle-name {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--principle-color);
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: 1.15rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.principle h2 {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6vw, 5rem);
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		line-height: 0.9;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.principle-inner > p:last-child {
		max-width: 34rem;
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--color-paper-muted);
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		line-height: 1.55;
	}

	.abilities {
		position: relative;
		isolation: isolate;
		min-height: 50rem;
		overflow: hidden;
		background: var(--color-indigo);
	}

	.abilities-art {
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0;
		z-index: -2;
	}

	.abilities-art img {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
	}

	.abilities-art img {
		object-fit: cover;
		object-position: 72% center;
	}

	.abilities::after {
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0;
		z-index: -1;
		background:
			linear-gradient(90deg, var(--color-indigo) 0%, rgb(27 33 64 / 94%) 48%, transparent 82%),
			linear-gradient(0deg, var(--color-indigo) 0%, transparent 30%);
		content: "";
	}

	.abilities-layout {
		display: flex;
		min-height: 50rem;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.abilities-content {
		max-width: 40rem;
	}

	.abilities-content .display-heading {
		max-width: 10ch;
	}

	.abilities-content .body-copy {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.4rem;
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
		color: var(--color-paper);
	}

	.consequences {
		display: grid;
		gap: 4rem;
	}

	.consequences-intro {
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	.consequence-list {
		margin: 0;
		border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-paper) 20%, transparent);
	}

	.consequence-list div {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding-block: 1.25rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-paper) 20%, transparent);
	}

	.consequence-list dt,
	.consequence-list dd {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
		font-weight: 600;
		line-height: 1;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.consequence-list dd {
		color: var(--color-acid);
		text-align: right;
	}

	.machinery {
		padding-block: var(--spacing-section);
		background: var(--color-paper);
		color: var(--color-night);
	}

	.machinery-layout {
		display: grid;
		gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
		align-items: center;
	}

	.machinery-art {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.machinery-art img {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
		object-fit: cover;
	}

	.machinery-art p {
		margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
		color: var(--color-tarmac);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.machinery-copy .body-copy {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.4rem;
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
		color: var(--color-tarmac);
	}

	.purpose {
		display: grid;
		gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
	}

	.purpose-question h2 {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: clamp(3rem, 6.5vw, 5.75rem);
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: -0.025em;
		line-height: 0.92;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.purpose-question span {
		color: var(--color-acid);
	}

	.purpose-copy {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.4rem;
	}

	.commitments {
		border-block: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-paper) 18%, transparent);
		background: var(--color-tarmac);
	}

	.commitments .display-heading {
		max-width: 10ch;
	}

	.commitment-grid {
		display: grid;
		margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.5rem);
		border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-paper) 24%, transparent);
	}

	.commitment-grid article {
		padding-block: 2rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-paper) 24%, transparent);
	}

	.commitment-grid h3 {
		max-width: 16ch;
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: 2rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		line-height: 1;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.commitment-grid p {
		max-width: 34rem;
		margin: 1rem 0 0;
		color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-paper) 78%, var(--color-tarmac));
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	.final-cta {
		position: relative;
		overflow: hidden;
		background: var(--color-acid);
		color: var(--color-night);
	}

	.final-cta::after {
		position: absolute;
		inset: -50% -10% auto auto;
		width: 34rem;
		height: 34rem;
		border: 8rem solid rgb(11 14 23 / 8%);
		border-radius: 50%;
		content: "";
	}

	.final-cta-inner {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 1;
		display: grid;
		gap: 2.5rem;
		align-items: end;
	}

	.final-cta .display-heading {
		max-width: 10ch;
	}

	.final-cta p {
		max-width: 40rem;
		margin: 2rem 0 0;
		font-size: 1.2rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	.final-cta .action-primary {
		border: 1px solid var(--color-night);
		background: var(--color-night);
		color: var(--color-paper);
	}

	.final-cta .action-primary:hover {
		background: var(--color-paper);
		color: var(--color-night);
	}

	@media (min-width: 48rem) {
		.concept {
			grid-template-columns: 0.95fr 1.05fr;
		}

		.principle-inner {
			grid-template-columns: 0.55fr 1fr 1fr;
			gap: 2rem;
		}

		.consequences {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		}

		.machinery-layout {
			grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr;
		}

		.purpose {
			grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr;
		}

		.commitment-grid {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		}

		.commitment-grid article {
			padding: 2.25rem;
			border-right: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-paper) 24%, transparent);
			border-bottom: 0;
		}

		.commitment-grid article:first-child {
			padding-left: 0;
		}

		.commitment-grid article:last-child {
			padding-right: 0;
			border-right: 0;
		}

		.final-cta-inner {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 47.99rem) {
		.abilities {
			min-height: auto;
		}

		.abilities-art {
			position: relative;
			height: 25rem;
		}

		.abilities::after {
			background: linear-gradient(0deg, var(--color-indigo) 0%, transparent 45%);
		}

		.abilities-layout {
			min-height: auto;
			padding-top: 3rem;
		}

		.consequence-list div {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 0.4rem;
		}

		.consequence-list dd {
			text-align: left;
		}
	}
</style>
